260	// What survives the retirement is the reason the mark is a LABEL at all: it must be
261	// appliable from the issue page on a phone, and it is write-gated by the platform —
262	// applying a label needs triage or write access — which is the first half of the
263	// security story (the second is the precondition's permission read at pickup,
264	// §16.4). The parameters that were labels are body fields now, gated on the
265	// author's push access instead (`parseRequestFields`).
